course: dictionary
lesson: 6524
title: Many meanings of nerve
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Nerve can name a part of the body, or it can mean courage, or it can mean rude boldness. Read the words around it to decide. «The funny bone is not a bone but a nerve running over the elbow close to the skin.» Here a nerve is a long thin fibre in the body.
explain: «It took nerve to jump off the high board.» Jumping from a high board is scary, so nerve must mean courage. When people say nerves, they usually mean worry. «Exam nerves made her hands shake» tells you she felt worried, not that her hands had a problem.
explain: «What a nerve!» is said when someone is rude or bold in a way that is not fair, like pushing in front of you in a queue. Here nerve means rude boldness. Always try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: A nerve is one of the long thin fibres that carry messages between the brain and other parts of the body.
fact: «Your brain is made of about 86 billion nerve cells» shows how many nerve cells help us think and move.
fact: Nerves help you feel pain or heat, so you can pull your hand away quickly.
fact: «Nerve» can mean courage: «It took nerve to jump», and «nerves» can mean feeling worried: «exam nerves».
fact: To «hold your nerve» means to stay calm and brave, and to «get on someone's nerves» means to annoy them.
exercise: «It took nerve to jump off the high board.» What does nerve mean here? | A tiny bone in the foot | *Courage to do something scary | A pain in the arm | Feeling sleepy
exercise: «The funny bone is a nerve running over the elbow.» What is a nerve in the body? | A type of food | Something that makes you sleepy | A kind of bone that cannot bend | *A long thin fibre that carries messages between the brain and other parts
exercise: «Exam nerves made her hands shake.» What does nerves mean here? | *Feeling worried | Feeling strong and happy | Feeling hungry | Feeling cold
test: «What a nerve!» someone says after a rude person pushes in front of a queue. What does nerve mean here? | Tiredness | Sadness | *Rude boldness | Kindness
test: Kai had to hold his nerve and keep going up the steep hill. What does hold your nerve mean? | Let go of the rope | Shout loudly for help | Run away quickly | *Stay calm and brave
exam: Which sentence uses nerve as a part of the body? | *«The funny bone is a nerve running over the elbow close to the skin.» | «It took nerve to climb the cliff.» | «Exam nerves made her shake.» | «What a nerve!»
